{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And he was afraid and said, etc.</b> Meaning: he felt in his heart that he was afraid of himself, and he said: how awesome is this place! And he gave a reason by saying <b>this is none other than the house of Elohim</b> — he was precise in using the name Elohim, for it is the source of fear, as it is written (Ecclesiastes 3:14): ״וְהָאֱלֹהִים עָשָׂה שֶׁיִּירְאוּ״ etc., and it is well known that the name Elohim instills dread in the human heart." "And his saying <b>and this is the gate</b> etc. — meaning: the place aligned opposite it, above, is the gate of heaven, and therefore he said a second time ״and this.״" "It further intends to give a reason for the surpassing greatness of the place, which changed above — ״this is none other than the house of Elohim״ — preceded by the definite article, for Yah chose for Himself a house to dwell there, and he said that it is this place. And he further proved that it is this, the house of choice, as he said: ״and this is the gate of heaven,״ for he saw that angels were ascending and descending, and the definite article preceded it for him — for the holy place is aligned opposite the gate of heaven."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:44:20.115661779Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}